1.10.1-snapshot
  The xnet HTTP client, the update check, game windows and hooks a mod starts
    The xnet module sends HTTP(S) requests through the winhttp.dll that Windows and Wine carry, and the update check uses it to find newer releases.
    A new module, xcui, builds X-Ray game windows from a layout, and xfs reaches real folders and files on disk.
    xlog's flush and xcreature's trader list start from the mod that uses them, xsound reads the mix loudness, and xlevel casts rays.

  xcui
    - Added the xcui module for X-Ray's game UI. build makes every control a layout lists, in draw order, and returns them by name.
      get_color, get_clipped, push_line, set_lines and is_close_key cover the colors, line lists and Esc that every window needs.
      get_list_place and set_list_place let a window reopen with its list where it was.

  xfs
    - Added read_disk_entries, read_drives, is_file, is_folder, create_folder and clone_file for real folders and files on disk.
      format_dir and get_parent_dir give a folder path the form these take and step up a folder, which a disk browser needs.
    - Added has_file, which tells whether the engine knows a file, and update_index, which rescans a mount after a mod writes one.
    - Changed remove_file to delete a file the engine has not indexed yet.
    - Added read_bytes, which reads the start of a file in binary mode.
    - Fixed read_folders, read_files and read_files_deep keeping the engine's file list in memory after every call.

  xnet
    - Brought back xnet with no exe. It makes HTTP(S) requests through the winhttp.dll that Windows and Wine already carry, called from Lua.
      run_request carries a request with a per-step timeout and an optional total budget, and push_github commits a file to a GitHub repo.

  Update check
    - Added the update check. On the first save load of each launch, each of my mods looks for a newer version of itself, during the loading screen.
      A newer version shows at the foot of that mod's MCM page, and in a PDA message once a day on entering the game, both naming moddb.
      Check for update in a mod's Development tab runs the same check right away.
    - Added get_update_status, the text and state of a mod's stored check for an update line in MCM, under the version line.
      run_update_check, show_update_check and show_update_news return what they did, for a mod's trace of each check.

  xsound
    - Added get_output_loudness, the loudness of the final mix the player hears, on modded exes that carry the mix meter. On other exes it reports the meter absent.
    - Added compute_spawn_dist, compute_spawn_pos and compute_channel_volume, vanilla's Lua channel placement and volume in one home.
    - Added get_channel_index, read_active_channels and get_ambient_state, which read the channel config and the channels in play the way vanilla does.
    - Added compute_verdict and format_play_detail, the audible-or-faint verdict and the acoustic tail of a trace line.
    - Added parse_blob, which reads an ogg's falloff from its bytes, and format_key, the canonical sound path key.
    - play_at takes a delay, a sound type and a falloff override.

  xlevel
    - Added find_ray_hit, one ray against the level's collision set. xcombat and xprops cast through it.
      It returns no surface normal on exes before 2026.4.13.
    - Changed get_neighbor_levels to follow the game graph on exes from 2026.10.11, so Meadow and added maps count. Older exes keep vanilla's level_links.

  xinventory
    - Changed the create_item docs to say that a requested cond, uses or condition range applies only to an item spawned online.

  xmcm
    - create_config returns a reset that puts every option back to its default and tells the mod's listeners.

  xlog
    - Added set_flush_level and apply_options to the logger, which take the log level and flush from a mod's options.
    - Changed the periodic flush and the lifecycle flushes to start from start_flush_hook, which each mod's dependency gate calls.
      xlog no longer registers a timer and callbacks by itself when a game loads.
      A mod without the gate still writes its log, and calls start_flush_hook from its on_game_start for the timed flushes.

  xpda
    - Added show_tip, a plain tip on the HUD.

  xcreature
    - Fixed iterate_online_monsters stopping after 400 objects, which skipped any monster past that point on a busy level.
    - Changed iterate_online to always walk db.storage, which every stalker and monster binder fills. The table no longer depends on load order, and a walk never visits inventory items.
    - Changed iterate_online_traders to need start_trader_hook, which a mod calls from the mod's on_game_start.
      xlibs no longer wraps db.add_obj on every load for every player, only when a mod uses the trader list.

  xcompat
    - Added the old names COMPASS and Nemesis Spawn System still call, so their location reads, retreats and flee runs work again on this xlibs.

1.10.0
  The xmonster mutant surface, cover finders, attachments and truer sight reads
    The new xmonster module covers mutant combat. It reads a mutant's state and memory, fires the jumps and attacks X-Ray validates, and sets its combat numbers.
    The xcombat cover finders pick a node by the score X-Ray's cover graph gives it, and reserve each pick in the vanilla cover ledger.
    get_facing reads the player's camera and a stalker's head, xinventory mounts attachments, and has_anomaly splits into hazard and artefact.

  xsmart
    - Added has_hazard_anomaly and is_hazard_anomaly_near for the fields that hurt, and has_artefact_anomaly and is_artefact_anomaly_near for the zones that spawn artefacts.
      They replace has_anomaly and is_anomaly_near.
    - Added is_service_npc, the test for a live trader, barman, medic or mechanic.
    - Fixed find_base_owner missing Sidorovich and the Forester and counting a dead seller. It reports Sidorovich's community as trader.
    - Improved find_base_owner performance.

  xcombat
    - Added get_best_cover, get_quick_cover and get_safe_cover, cover finders that score a node the way X-Ray's cover graph does. They replace find_cover.
      get_best_cover picks the most hidden node toward a threat, get_quick_cover the nearest decent one, and get_safe_cover a spot walled all round.
      Each pick is reserved in the vanilla cover ledger. NPCs never stack on a cover, and vanilla's cover schemes see the claim.
    - Added is_concealed and the COVER_FLOOR levels, the test the cover finders score a node by.
    - Changed find_flee_lane to the name find_free_lane.
    - Added get_combat_action, the action the combat planner runs now, such as kill_enemy or take_cover.
    - Added is_enemy_watching, true when the enemy holds a weapon and has the combatant in his sight, and is_enemy_above for an enemy on a rock or ledge.
    - Added is_off_navmesh and is_point_off_navmesh for a body or a point off the AI graph, and get_actor_velocity, which answers only for the player.
    - Changed get_facing and is_in_sight to follow where the player looks, from the camera, and where a stalker aims, from his head.
    - Changed is_in_sight to trace from the viewer's eye to the target's center. A crosshair anywhere on the body counts, and a low wall hides a dog behind it.
    - Changed get_weapon_kind to take a hands-only flag, which reads a holstered player as unarmed, and to return nil for a mutant.
    - Fixed on_cover_repick registering under a callback id X-Ray rejects. The cover re-pick veto attaches again.

  xmonster
    - Added xmonster, the mutant combat surface over the modded exes' monster hooks. Each call probes its hook once and stays inert on an exe without it.
      Reads cover a mutant's state, morale, health, its memory of hits, sounds and its enemy, and the time since it last sensed that enemy.
      Invokes fire a jump under the checks X-Ray gives its jumps, a rotation jump, a run attack and a threat display, and return false on a refusal.
      Setters write the per-mutant combat numbers and species abilities, arm the rear spin strike, override an animation, and hook the mutant's combat decision.

  xgraft
    - Fixed register_takeover attaching before a stalker's logic was set up. It returns false until the logic is ready, and the caller retries.
    - Fixed apply_takeover_block blocking the wrong action when a stalker lacks one of the blocked planners.

  xcreature
    - Added is_companion, the player's companion check for one NPC, online or offline.
    - Added is_wounded, vanilla's wounded test, cheap enough to ask of every stalker on every pass.
    - Added iterate_online_traders for Sidorovich and the Forester, the trader-class NPCs that db.OnlineStalkers never lists.
    - Fixed is_unscriptable keeping a stalker's companion status from before the player recruited him.

  xinventory
    - Added the attachment category for silencers, scopes and grenade launchers. A policy caps them on a separate row, where they used to count against the weapon cap.
    - Added can_add_attachment, get_fitting_attachments and try_add_attachment, which check what fits an NPC's gun and mount it.
      A scope swaps the gun for its scoped variant, and try_add_attachment returns the new id.
    - Added attachment_slot_2 and attachment_slot_3, a loose attachment that fits the NPC's pistol or rifle, resolved like ammo.

  xttltable
    - Changed the TTL table load to take an expiry function. A saved row keeps its real lifetime, where load used to give every saved row a fresh one.
    - Removed the per-event metadata from the sliding-window counter.
    - Improved sliding-window counter performance.

  xmath
    - Added shuffle_back, an in-place Fisher-Yates shuffle that works from the back of the array.

  xsound
    - Fixed play_at stopping every timer in the game until the next load, when a sound got no voice.
    - Changed compute_delivered_loudness to follow X-Ray's gain chain and take the script volume. It read too loud on sounds lifted past the clamp.

  ximplot
    - Added ximplot, a wrapper over the modded exes' ImPlot bind that stays inert on an exe without it.

  xcompat
    - Added xcompat, the home for aliases that keep a released mod running across an xlibs API change. It keeps has_anomaly for AlifePlus 1.8.9.

1.9.1
  The xpda last-news clock for a PDA quiet window
    A mod can now hold its PDA line back while another mod's line is still fresh.

  - Added start_news_hook and get_last_news in xpda, a shared clock of the last PDA line from any mod.
    start_news_hook wraps the vanilla send_tip sinks, and every drawn line stamps the clock. publish_news and npc_tip stamp it too.

1.9.0
  The xgraft, xfs and xltx modules, engine hook wrappers, and verb-first names
    The new xgraft module holds the GOAP takeover, xfs the file reads and writes, and xltx the LTX reads that survive a missing key.
    xcombat and xsound wrap new X-Ray hooks for the hit redirect, the visible-enemy bias, the movement hold, the combat-distance asks and ambient sound.
    Public functions across the library take verb-first names, listed old to new under each module, with no alias left for the old names.

  xsquad
    - Added is_last_man, true for a squadless stalker or the last living member of his squad.
    - Added format_squad_record, the one-line record of a squad, which format_squads now prints for every squad.
    - Changed the names acquire_squad to set_target_smart, dump_squads to format_squads, get_squad_by_member to get_member_squad, iter_member_ids to iterate_member_ids, iter_squads to iterate_squads,
      reassert_target to set_target, and target_actor to set_target_actor.

  xsmart
    - Added remove_npc_role, which forgets one NPC's cached service roles when he is released.
    - Removed has_jobs_for. get_npc_job reads the job a stalker holds.
    - Changed the names accepts_faction to can_accept_faction, anomaly_near to is_anomaly_near, base_owner_near to find_base_owner, dump_smarts to format_smarts,
      get_faction_smart_count to get_faction_count, get_job_for_npc to get_npc_job, get_mechanic_at_smart to get_smart_mechanic, get_medic_at_smart to get_smart_medic,
      get_section_npc_max to get_section_max, get_section_npc_range to get_section_range, get_trader_at_smart to get_smart_trader, has_animated_stalker_jobs to has_animated_jobs,
      has_mechanic_at_smart to has_smart_mechanic, has_medic_at_smart to has_smart_medic, has_squad_of_faction to has_faction_squad, has_trader_at_smart to has_smart_trader,
      iter_stationed_squads to iterate_stationed_squads, reconcile_squad_roster to update_squad_roster, section_faction to get_section_faction, smart_iter to iterate_smarts,
      and smarts_by_names to get_named_smarts.

  xsmart_spawn
    - Changed the names get_tiered_faction_squads to get_tiered_squads, repopulate to reset_population, set_exclusive_spawn_section to set_exclusive_section,
      set_exclusive_spawn_tiered to set_exclusive_tiered, and set_shared_spawn_section to set_shared_section.

  xstash
    - Changed the names fill_stash to add_stash_items and loot_stash to collect_stash_items.

  xlevel
    - Changed the names cell_key to build_cell_key, get_actor_level_id to get_actor_level, get_level_id_by_name to resolve_level_id, and get_smart_display_name to get_smart_name.

  xcombat
    - Added set_hit_redirect, which turns a hit stalker's target selection toward a close attacker.
    - Added set_visible_enemy_bias, which sets per NPC how strongly he picks the enemy that sees him, the player and NPCs apart.
    - Added set_movement_hold, which keeps a stalker planted with his path kept until the caller clears it.
    - Added on_get_min_combat_dist and on_get_max_combat_dist, which register a handler on X-Ray's cover-band asks with its weapon-typed base to scale.
    - Added get_block_reason, the reason a combatant cannot fire now, unarmed, reloading or an empty magazine, and is_unarmed and is_magazine_empty.
    - Added is_in_sight, the sight test for any viewer and cone. It replaces actor_can_hit.
    - Added is_facing, get_range_band, is_bleeding, get_best_enemy, has_body_in_lane, has_wall_between, is_actor_sprinting and is_actor_climbing.
    - Changed get_operator to name the generic scheme operators, such as rx_ff and fight_from_cover.
    - Changed can_see to return false for a dead NPC without an X-Ray error in the log.
    - Changed the names actor_dist_sqr to get_actor_dist, body_busy to is_body_busy, claim_cover to register_cover, disclose_enemy to show_enemy, enclosure to get_enclosure_state,
      has_friendly_in_line to has_friendly_lane, has_obstacle_to_target to has_shot_obstacle, scale_dispersion to apply_dispersion, scale_hit_power to apply_hit_power, sees to can_see,
      sees_within to can_see_within, and send_to to set_destination.

  xgraft
    - Added xgraft, the GOAP takeover moved out of xcombat. install_takeover is now register_takeover, and topup_takeover_block is apply_takeover_block.
      is_takeover_current, release_takeover, release_takeover_id and get_blocked_planners keep their names under xgraft.

  xcreature
    - Added is_zombied, the zombied stalker community, not the zombie mutant.
    - Fixed relation and get_actor_relation raising a Lua error on an object that is not a creature, such as a grenade. They return nil.
    - Changed the names any_human_online to has_online_human, any_mutant_online to has_online_mutant, attach_particle to start_particle, community to get_community,
      goodwill_to_actor to get_actor_goodwill, is_enemy_to_actor to is_actor_enemy, make_trader to create_trader, online_iter_with_id to iterate_online,
      online_monster_iter to iterate_online_monsters, and relation_to_actor to get_actor_relation.

  xobject
    - Changed the names go to get_go and se to get_se.

  xactor
    - Changed the name give_info to add_info_portion.

  xinventory
    - Added collect_surplus, which counts an NPC's inventory and releases its surplus in one walk.
    - Changed the names classify to collect_policy_counts, deny_move to disable_move, dump to log_inventory, get_ammo_tier_map to get_ammo_tiers, and policy_key to get_policy_key.

  xtable
    - Added clone, a shallow copy of a table.
    - Changed the name count to get_count.

  xttltable
    - Changed the names table:all to get_all, table:size to get_size, table:remaining_ttl to get_remaining_ttl, table:export to get_snapshot, table:import to load, counter:all to get_all,
      counter:count to get_count, counter:export to get_snapshot, counter:import to load, bucket:acquire to get_token, bucket:peek to check, fifo:size to get_size, and fifo:each to iterate.

  xmath
    - Added is_in_range, a ground-plane distance test against a radius.
    - Changed the names dist_flat_sqr to get_flat_dist, partial_shuffle to shuffle_partial, sample to select, and sample_n to select_n.

  xslice
    - Changed the name cancel to stop_queue.

  xstring
    - Changed the name interpolate to format_template.

  xtime
    - Changed the names game_sec to get_game_sec, game_time to get_game_time, and hms to get_time_hm.

  xconst
    - Added the COMMUNITY, RELATION and TASK_STATUS constant tables.

  xfs
    - Added xfs, the file system module. read_folders, read_files and read_files_deep list the engine file system, and read_file and write_file read and write a real path.
      remove_file deletes through the engine file system, because os.remove is absent from the game's Lua, and resolve_path turns a mount path into a full one.

  xltx
    - Added xltx, LTX reads that stay safe when a section or key is missing, as maps, lists and typed fields from a path or an open file.

  xinspect
    - Changed the name userdata to format_userdata.

  xpp
    - Changed the names acquire to create_effector and inspect to get_snapshot.

  xsound
    - Added register_ambient_listener and unregister_ambient_listener on the X-Ray ambient sound hooks for the weather bed, music, script sounds, effects, thunder and rain.
      Each listener returns a volume factor, and 0 silences the play. Several mods can listen to the same hook.
    - Added play_at, stop_shot and stop_shots, a single sound the caller can stop.
    - Added load_meta, get_meta and compute_delivered_loudness, a registry of measured sound data and the loudness of one play at a distance.
    - Changed the names acquire to create_sound and inspect to get_snapshot.

  xevent
    - Changed the name hook to register_hook.

  xpda
    - Changed the names mark_entity to add_entity_marker, mark_squad to add_squad_marker, npc_tip to show_npc_tip, send to publish_news, unmark_entity to remove_entity_marker,
      and unmark_squad to remove_squad_marker.

  xprops
    - Changed the names ground_below to find_ground and place to spawn_object.

  Performance
    - Improved performance across the library, profiled with JitProfiler.

1.8.5
  The xprops module, cover reads, combat writes and inventory walk caps
    The new xprops module places world props on an online level, snapped to the ground and checked for collision.
    xcombat reads the baked cover graph by direction at crouch and standing height, picks the nearest or best cover in find_cover, and writes health, hit power and shot spread.
    is_task_target covers a quest objective, the spawn writers drop sections the game cannot spawn, and xtrace keeps only its id.

  xsquad
    - Changed is_task_target to protect a squad that an active task marks as its objective, or that has a member marked so. get_active_task_targets returns those ids.

  xsmart
    - Added anomaly_near, true when an anomaly sits within a radius of a position, and base_owner_near, the faction of the nearest base seller.
    - Changed get_declared_factions to public, the factions a smart's props declare.
    - Changed has_campfire to answer offline map campfires from xdata.campfire_smarts. Removed note_campfire_object and campfire_map_count.
    - Fixed clear_npc_job leaving the NPC in the smart's job occupancy, which could keep other NPCs from that job.

  xsmart_spawn
    - Added get_tiered_faction_squads, a faction's squad pool capped by the level's danger tier. set_exclusive_spawn_tiered resolves its pool through it.
    - Changed set_exclusive_spawn_section to accept an array of squad sections, and the game picks one per spawn.
    - Changed the spawn writers to drop squad sections the system ini lacks, and to write no row when none is left.
    - Removed add_runtime_job and remove_runtime_job.

  xdata
    - Added campfire_smarts, the base Anomaly smarts with a map-placed campfire.

  xcombat
    - Added get_crouch_openness and get_stand_openness, how open the baked cover graph is toward a direction at each height. They read static geometry and see no bodies.
    - Changed find_cover to take opts for nearest or best cover, firing from it or hiding in it, a radius and a search position. The search_pos argument is gone.
    - Removed find_shot.
    - Added is_line_blocked and the BODY_Y heights, the object-aware clearance ray. has_obstacle_to_target casts from the shooter's eye height.
    - Added sees_within, which tests the distance before the sight read.
    - Added get_health_frac and add_health_frac, an NPC's health as a fraction and a clamped change to it.
    - Added scale_hit_power and scale_dispersion, which scale a pending hit and a shot's spread and compose with other callers.
    - Added set_view_distance_factor and set_health_restore_boost, an NPC's sight range and passive regeneration, inert on an exe without the bind.
    - Added get_facing, get_enclosure and enclosure, which reads outdoor, indoor or underground. is_indoor reads get_enclosure.
    - Changed set_aim_params to assert on an angle above PI, where X-Ray's tracking band stops working.
    - Changed TAKEOVER_ID from 188200 to 188347. The old id collided with a companion mod's surge-shelter scheme, and a consumer reads TAKEOVER_ID.

  xcreature
    - Added attach_particle, which attaches a particle to a creature's bone and checks the bone first. It has no detach, and the particle dies with the object.
    - Added online_monster_iter, any_human_online and any_mutant_online.
    - Added relation, is_enemy, relation_to_actor, is_enemy_to_actor and goodwill_to_actor.
    - Added RANK_TIERS, the ordered rank names, novice first.

  xinventory
    - Added an optional max_items cap to iterate_inventory, classify and iterate_surplus. The walk stops there and returns true as its second value.

  xtrace
    - Removed push and pop. A trace carries its id only.

  xsound
    - Added length, a sound's duration read without playing it.
    - Fixed play letting the garbage collector cut a sound short.

  xprops
    - Added xprops with place, remove, ground_below and is_clear.

  xpda, xstash
    - Fixed a map mark crashing the game during a level change. A mark call now returns whether the mark is really on the map.

1.8.4
  Takeover blocking, stagger and flinch reads, position guards, and the dev version
    The takeover now blocks every top-level action that competes with it, tops the block up at each seize, and exports TAKEOVER_ID for state_mgr.
    xcombat reads a stagger, a hit flinch and a busy body, and the spatial queries reject a position that is not a vector.
    is_compatible accepts the "next" dev version, and set_combat no longer leaves a seized stalker staring at his old enemy.

  xsmart
    - Added clear_npc_job, which clears the job fields select_npc_job reads. The smart assigns a new job on its next pass.

  xsmart_spawn
    - Fixed add_runtime_job leaving a generated job's ini out of db.dynamic_ltx. A save that kept the job crashed the game on load.

  xcombat
    - Changed install_takeover to block every top-level action that can compete with the takeover, where it used to block a short list.
    - Added topup_takeover_block, which blocks an action the stalker's manager gained after the graft. A consumer runs it at each seize.
    - Added is_takeover_current, true while the takeover action is the manager's current top-level action.
    - Added TAKEOVER_ID, the takeover action's GOAP id, for a consumer to declare in state_mgr.combat_action_ids.
    - Added an on_release callback to the takeover spec, and get_operator names the takeover.
    - Added body_busy, true while a stagger, a script animation or a hit flinch holds the body. Its second value names which one.
    - Added is_staggering and is_flinching. is_staggering wraps critically_wounded, the short critical-hit stagger and not the wounded state.
    - Added get_sight_target, the object and mode the sight manager holds.
    - Changed find_flee_lane to check its last-resort lane for obstacles, and to return nil when no lane is clear.
    - Fixed a seized stalker staying aimed at his previous enemy and never firing. set_combat sets the sight on the committed target on every fire order.

  xactor
    - Added get_talking_npc, the NPC the player trades or talks with.

  xinventory
    - Added dump, one log line of an NPC's inventory counts per section. The caller gates it on a debug flag.

  xmath
    - Added check_pos, a guard against a position that is not a vector. A mod that shadows an object's position no longer crashes the spatial queries.
      find_smart, find_friendly_base, is_near_campfire, find_squad, find_squads, has_squad, find_stashes, cell_key and is_indoor run it.

  xlibs
    - Changed is_compatible to accept the "next" dev version, which sorts above every release of its API major. A "next" xlibs used to refuse every mod.

1.8.3
  Reload events, level danger tiers, spawn section injection and runtime jobs
    The xcombat module wraps the reload start and stop events, reads a reload, and lets set_combat hold fire through it.
    The xlevel module rates each level's danger, and xsmart_spawn injects a named squad section, a tiered faction pool or a whole job into a smart.
    Other additions are make_trader, is_monster_faction, cell_key and xobject.release, and set_fire_queue_scale scales an NPC's bursts.

  xsmart
    - Added get_section_npc_range, both bounds of a squad section's npc_in_squad, cached.
    - Changed has_campfire to check a static map campfire set first, fed by note_campfire_object. Added campfire_map_count.

  xsmart_spawn
    - Added set_shared_spawn_section, which injects a named squad section into a smart's respawn.
    - Added set_exclusive_spawn_section, the same inject tagged with the smart's owner faction. It passes the faction gate of an exclusive smart.
    - Added set_exclusive_spawn_tiered, the exclusive faction inject with its squad tiers capped by the level's danger tier.
    - Added add_runtime_job and remove_runtime_job, which push a job into a smart's job list from the caller's logic and pull it out again, freeing its NPC.

  xlevel
    - Added DANGER_TIER and get_danger_tier, a danger tier per level from the rookie maps to the endgame. An unknown level reads DANGER_TIER_DEFAULT, the mid tier.
    - Added cell_key, the shared density cell for a position. Separate density checks then agree on what one area is.

  xcombat
    - Added on_reload_start and on_reload_stop, which register on the NPC reload events and return false on an exe without them.
    - Added is_reloading, the reload read from the active weapon's state, on every exe.
    - Added actor_can_hit, true when the player holds a firearm, faces the NPC within a cone and has a clear shot line.
    - Added set_fire_queue_scale, which scales an NPC's burst size and pause in the combat planner, inert on an exe without the bind.
    - Changed set_combat to hold a fire order as READY while the NPC reloads. A fire order mid-reload used to cancel the reload.
    - Changed set_combat to leave sniper_fire_mode off for a SNIPE order. That flag aimed the shot at the sight target and dropped recoil.
    - Changed disclose_enemy to put the shooter in the victim's seen memory where the exe has make_enemy_visible. The victim then turns on him.

  xcreature
    - Added is_monster_faction, true for a monster squad faction.
    - Added make_trader, which makes an online NPC a working trader from a vanilla trade config and leaves his community alone.

  xobject
    - Added release, a wrapper over alife_release that refuses a nil object.

1.8.2
  Fire discipline in set_combat, fire queue bands and the cover re-pick veto
    The set_combat call takes a fire intent and the enemy, and holds fire as READY when no shot makes sense.
    The xcombat module carries the engine's burst bands per weapon and range, and registers on the cover re-pick veto.
    Other additions are get_faction_smart_count, is_companion, remove_squad, is_unscriptable_se and dist_flat_sqr, and spawnable ammo pools skip broken sections.

  xsquad
    - Added is_companion, true for an active companion squad. has_active_role and is_protected read it.
    - Added remove_squad, a wrapper over SIMBOARD:remove_squad.

  xsmart
    - Added get_faction_smart_count, the smarts on a level that hold a stationed squad of a community or of any in a set.

  xcombat
    - Changed set_combat to take a fire intent and the enemy, and to hold fire as READY when no shot makes sense. The caller holds no fire logic.
    - Added FIRE_QUEUE and get_fire_queue, the engine's burst size and interval bounds per weapon kind and range band.
    - Added on_cover_repick, which lets a handler keep an NPC on his current cover when X-Ray finds a new one. It registers only where the exe has the hook.

  xcreature
    - Added is_unscriptable_se, the is_unscriptable check for a server entity, online or offline.

  xinventory
    - Fixed the ammo category holding sections without k_ap. Spawning one crashed the game.

  xmath
    - Added dist_flat_sqr, the squared ground-plane distance between positions.

  xmcm
    - Removed platform_functor and platform_status. The xlibs MCM page builds the status line itself.

1.8.1
  Engine fire-gate wrappers, the roster reconcile, and a cut of unused exports
    The xcombat module wraps the per-NPC combat binds of the modded exes, aim, vision speed, shot clearance, fire sense and the action switch veto, each with a fallback below the bind.
    Every export with no consumer is gone, listed per module under Removed.
    Other changes are the xsmart roster reconcile, the xmcm platform status, the xlog flush timer and get_name for mutants in the player's language.

  xsquad
    - Added collect_squad_ids, every SIMBOARD squad id in a reusable array, for a squad walk spread across frames.
    - Added create_squad, which spawns a squad at a smart through the vanilla board path.

  xsmart
    - Added reconcile_squad_roster, which syncs the SIMBOARD rosters after a squad changed smart through the vanilla assign_smart.
    - Changed find_friendly_base to take a min_distance filter.
    - Fixed get_npc_roles giving a dead NPC's roles to the next holder of his id. A cache entry now checks the NPC's section.
    - Removed get_npc_for_job. get_declared_factions is now internal.

  xstash
    - Removed is_stash_available, mark_stash_looted and clear_stash.

  xlevel
    - Removed get_game_hours and get_location_name.

  xcombat
    - Added set_aim_params, set_vision_speed, can_kill_enemy, can_kill_member, fire_make_sense and on_action_switch over the modded exes' combat binds.
      Each probes its bind on the first call and falls back to a defined result below it.
    - Added sees, the seen-now read that vanilla kill_enemy fires on, and get_cover_state, the combat planner's cover flags.
    - Added is_under_fire, true when the enemy hit or shot at the NPC inside a window.
    - Added resolve_enemy, a remembered enemy id as a live object, and actor_dist_sqr, the cached squared distance to the player.
    - Added has_obstacle_to_target, the object-aware shot line. It replaces has_occluder_between, which saw walls only.
    - Added release_takeover_id, which releases a takeover by id after the NPC is gone.
    - Changed install_takeover to assert on a second, different spec instead of replacing the first consumer's policy.
    - Changed find_flee_lane to try a half-length fan before the short straight lane.
    - Changed is_indoor to test for a roof and walls by ray, where it used to read the distance to a surge shelter.
    - Changed set_combat to aim a fleeing NPC down his run path. He used to keep staring at the shooter and run backwards.
    - Changed get_operator to name every vanilla action id.
    - Fixed get_weapon_kind reading a slung rifle while the NPC fired his pistol. It reads the item in his hands first.
    - Fixed a seized NPC keeping a script animation, such as a limp, and sliding while the maneuver moved him.
    - Fixed send_to returning the invalid vertex when no accessible node was near. It falls back to the node the NPC stands on.
    - Removed resolve_stance, find_point and AGGRESSOR_KINDS.

  xcreature
    - Changed get_name to prefer a mutant's translated name over the built-in English one, cached per section.
    - Changed get_name to return nil for a nil entity or a nameless stalker, and the caller picks the fallback.
    - Removed query and its iterator, entity_type, pos, online_iter, get_goodwill and set_goodwill. get_clsid is now internal.

  xtable
    - Removed is_array, clone, filter, find, reduce, sweep, bisect_left, binary_insert, memoize, acquire_lock, check_lock and clear_locks.

  xttltable
    - Fixed a TTL table returning nil for a stored false. A false now round-trips, as in the FIFO cache.
    - Removed create_budget.

  xmath
    - Removed chance, prd_chance, prd_reset, weighted_choice and vary.

  xstring
    - Removed capitalize_first.

  xconst
    - Added INVALID_BONE_ID.

  xlog
    - Fixed the periodic flush firing once per session. The timer re-arms, and buffered lines reach the disk on the set interval.

  xprofiler
    - Removed wrap.

  xtrace
    - Removed wrap and reset.

  xinspect
    - Removed inspect. get_type is now internal.

  xbus
    - Removed unsubscribe, get_subscribers, count, has, stats, reset_stats and debug_state.

  xevent
    - Removed unhook, emit and list_hooks.

  xpda
    - Removed hydrate_markers.

  xmcm
    - Added platform_status and platform_functor, the xlibs, xray-monolith and AOEngine versions as a status line for an MCM footer.
    - Removed create_loader, extract_defaults, format_defaults and format_config. create_getter is now internal to create_config.

  xlibs_mcm
    - Removed set_version_text. The page footer reads the platform status.

1.8.0
  The GOAP takeover graft, the flee lane, and combat state reads
    The xcombat module grafts a takeover onto a stalker's GOAP planner, with its block list, the squad combat-mask calls and an arrival read.
    It also finds a flee lane down a clear path, and reads the brain's operator, the body's turn off a target and an enemy's last known position.
    Other changes are find_friendly_base, is_near_campfire, get_rank_chance, is_surge, is_story, and fixes to get_clsid and create_item.

  xsquad
    - Added get_community, a squad's raw community id, the untranslated get_community_name.

  xsmart
    - Added find_friendly_base, the nearest base not held by an enemy of a community.
    - Added get_job_for_npc, the job an NPC holds at a smart.
    - Added is_near_campfire, true when a position is near a campfire bound to the smart. It tells a real fire seat from the campfire_point fallback.

  xlevel
    - Added is_surge, true while a surge or psi storm is underway.

  xcombat
    - Added install_takeover, release_takeover and get_blocked_planners, the GOAP graft that holds a stalker for a script while its gate is up.
    - Added register_in_combat and unregister_in_combat, the squad memory-sharing mask the blocked combat planner no longer sets.
    - Added is_arrived, true once the NPC's path is complete.
    - Added find_flee_lane, a flee destination down a lane clear of geometry and objects.
    - Added get_operator, the combat operator the brain runs now, and get_facing_offset, how far the body is turned off a position.
    - Added has_obstacle_between, the object-aware movement lane ray.
    - Changed enemy_track_pos to the name get_track_pos and enemy_unseen_ms to the name get_unseen_ms. Removed aim_at.
    - Changed set_combat's READY matrix to carry the raid, assault and sneak states.
    - Changed the sniper weapon band to start closer. A sniper now fights at mid range.

  xcreature
    - Fixed get_clsid reading a low entity id as a class id. is_npc, is_stalker and is_mutant gave wrong answers for early story NPCs.

  xobject
    - Added is_story, true for an entity that carries a story id.

  xinventory
    - Added get_rank_chance, an item section's chance to appear by the player's rank tier, with a category floor and cost bands.
    - Added release_item_id, which releases an item by id, offline too.
    - Added get_item_name, an item section's display name.
    - Fixed create_item dropping the condition on weapons, outfits and helmets. They spawned at full condition.

1.7.7
  The xcombat module, personal goodwill, the NPC tip and section policy rows
    The new xcombat module carries the combat primitives for a script-driven NPC: weapon kind and range, enemy memory, cover and shot finders, a combat-state matrix and movement.
    Policy rows in xinventory key on an item section as well as a category, and a corpse-take veto guards the loot menu.
    Other additions are personal goodwill in xcreature, an id-yielding online iterator and the NPC tip in xpda.

  xsmart_spawn
    - Removed the empty on_game_start.

  xcombat
    - Added xcombat with get_weapon_kind, get_weapon_range and WEAPON_RANGES, the weapon kind and its fight range.
      enemy_track_pos and enemy_unseen_ms read enemy memory, and disclose_enemy makes an NPC register a known enemy.
      find_cover, find_shot and find_point search rings for cover and a shot, and claim_cover and release_cover reserve a cover node.
      set_combat drives weapon, posture and movement through a combat-state matrix, send_to moves the NPC, and resolve_stance, aim_at, is_indoor and get_squad_ordinal complete it.

  xcreature
    - Added get_goodwill and set_goodwill over the personal relation registry. set_goodwill changes one NPC's attitude to another and leaves the communities alone.
    - Added online_iter_with_id, which yields id and object. A caller can check the server object before using a game object that is being destroyed.

  xinventory
    - Added section policy rows. A policy row names a category or an item section, and an item takes its section's rule first. policy_key picks the row.
    - Changed get_equipped_ids to leave out the grenade slot. The policy manages a slotted grenade.
    - Added is_corpse_take and deny_move for ActorMenu_on_item_before_move. One tells a take from a dead body, the other vetoes the move.
    - Removed get_ammo_count, get_ammo_classes and get_ammo_tier. get_ammo_sections, get_ammo_tier_map and resolve_ammo_category remain.

  xpda
    - Added npc_tip, a PDA tip from an NPC, with his name, his portrait and a PDA sound.

1.7.6
  The xsquad squad class check
    The new is_squad check tells a real squad from another object that took a recycled id.

  - Added is_squad in xsquad, true only for a sim_squad_scripted object.
  - Fixed assign_squad_to_smart in xsmart calling assign_smart on an object that is not a squad. It checks is_squad first.

